m the very beginning,\r\n49: [00:13:12 -> 00:13:15] according to His for knowledge, allows us,\r\n50: [00:13:15 -> 00:13:18] mortal flesh, to move His hand through prayer.\r\n51: [00:13:18 -> 00:13:21] It's a mystery that we will only understand fully in heaven.\r\n52: [00:13:21 -> 00:13:23] But we're commanded to pray.\r\n53: [00:13:23 -> 00:13:26] We're told to pray and to pray with faith,\r\n54: [00:13:26 -> 00:13:28] without trying to understand it with our own eyes\r\n55: [00:13:28 -> 00:13:32] and our own minds and to believe that God hears\r\n56: [00:13:32 -> 00:13:33] an answer to prayer.\r\n57: [00:13:33 -> 00:13:37] He hears prayer, brothers, sisters, children, young people.\r\n58: [00:13:37 -> 00:13:39] God hears prayer.\r\n59: [00:13:39 -> 00:13:40] He has hears that we can hear,\r\n60: [00:13:40 -> 00:13:43] we're not praying to an idol or a stone.\r\n61: [00:13:43 -> 00:13:46] Have you treated the God of heaven who is living\r\n62: [00:13:46 -> 00:13:49] like a stone idol who has no ears\r\n63: [00:13:49 -> 00:13:51] and who has no eyes to see?\r\n64: [00:13:51 -> 00:13:53] No mouth to speak.\r\n65: [00:13:53 -> 00:13:54] We serve a living God.\r\n66: [00:13:54 -> 00:13:58] Jesus is alive and he ever lives to intercede for us.\r\n67: [00:13:58 -> 00:14:00] He is praying.\r\n68: [00:14:00 -> 00:14:01] He is praying for you.\r\n69: [00:14:01 -> 00:14:03] There at the right hand of the Father.\r\n70: [00:14:03 -> 00:14:05] He's interceding for you.\r\n71: [00:14:05 -> 00:14:07] Join him in that prayer that He's praying for you.\r\n72: [00:14:07 -> 00:14:10] Join him in the prayer that He's praying for others\r\n73: [00:14:10 -> 00:14:12] in your circle of influence.\r\n74: [00:14:12 -> 00:14:15] Is there something, think about the most impossible\r\n75: [00:14:15 -> 00:14:17] seeming circumstance?\r\n76: [00:14:17 -> 00:14:20] The one that seems hopeless, the one that seems like it's\r\n77: [00:14:20 -> 00:14:23] dead and buried, three days buried.\r\n78: