n, that I've been carrying\r\n105: [00:15:46 -> 00:15:48] all this time, I laid at your feet and believe\r\n106: [00:15:48 -> 00:15:49] that you will untangle the knots.\r\n107: [00:15:49 -> 00:15:54] Jesus Christ came to untangle the knots of your life.\r\n108: [00:15:54 -> 00:15:55] And He will do that.\r\n109: [00:15:55 -> 00:15:57] He came.\r\n110: [00:15:57 -> 00:16:00] He came to destroy the works of the devil.\r\n111: [00:16:00 -> 00:16:02] And He's doing that.\r\n112: [00:16:02 -> 00:16:03] He will do that.\r\n113: [00:16:03 -> 00:16:04] He is done it on the cross.\r\n114: [00:16:04 -> 00:16:07] He's done it through the triumphing over the grave.\r\n115: [00:16:07 -> 00:16:09] And He's done it because He's seated at the right hand\r\n116: [00:16:09 -> 00:16:10] of the Father.\r\n117: [00:16:10 -> 00:16:12] And all authority has been given to Him\r\n118: [00:16:12 -> 00:16:13] in heaven and on earth.\r\n119: [00:16:13 -> 00:16:17] And that includes hell and all the hosts of hell, Satan\r\n120: [00:16:17 -> 00:16:20] Himself who has been defeated.\r\n121: [00:16:20 -> 00:16:23] And the God of peace shall soon crush Satan under your feet.\r\n122: [00:16:23 -> 00:16:26] These are the promises He's given us, church family.\r\n123: [00:16:26 -> 00:16:28] May we confess it, may we put our hope in it.\r\n124: [00:16:28 -> 00:16:30] This is the only thing that's worth putting our hope in,\r\n125: [00:16:30 -> 00:16:34] not our bank accounts, not our homes, not our earthly security.\r\n126: [00:16:34 -> 00:16:37] He's but the Word of God, His promises shall never fail.\r\n127: [00:16:37 -> 00:16:40] Heaven and earth shall pass away.\r\n128: [00:16:40 -> 00:16:43] But His words will never pass away.\r\n129: [00:16:43 -> 00:16:45] So lay your burden at His feet.\r\n130: [00:16:45 -> 00:16:47] Whatever it is.\r\n131: [00:16:47 -> 00:16:49] Perhaps you brought one burden today.\r\n132: [00:16:49 -> 00:16:50] That's one too many.\r\n133: [00:16:50 -> 00:16:54] And if you're carrying 10, lay them all at His feet.\r\n134: [00:16:54 -> 00:16:55] Heavenly Father, we come in our lives to you.\r\n135: [00:16:55 -> 00:16:59] We thank you that you're a God who specializes\r\n136: [00:16:59 -> 00:17:00] in the impossible.\r\n137: [00:17:00 -> 00:17:03] Your specializes in those things that are dead,\r\n138: [00:17:03 -> 00:17:04] that you might bring Him back to life\r\n139: [00:17:04 -> 00:17:06] so that our confidence will not be in ourselves.\r\n140: [00:17:06 -> 00:17:09] So thank you all that You've allowed us to reach places\r\n141: [00:17:09 -> 00:17:12] of hopelessness, places of death even\r\n142: [00:17:12 -> 00:17:14] so that You alone could be our hope.\r\n143: [00:17:14 -> 00:17:16] Where we know that there's no other hope,\r\n144: [00:17:16 -> 00:17:18] except that Your resurrection power bring us back to life.\r\n145: [00:17:18 -> 00:17:21] So Lord, I pray for that for myself\r\n146: [00:17:21 -> 00:17:23] and for everyone here, Lord, in this room\r\n147: [00:17:23 -> 00:17:24] and listening online.\r\n148: [00:17:24 -> 00:17:27] I pray, Lord, that Your power will be manifest.\r\n149: [00:17:27 -> 00:17:31] Thank You that Your power shows up best in weakness.\r\n150: [00:17:31 -> 00:17:34] Lord, we bring to You our areas of weakness\r\n151: [00:17:34 -> 00:17:37] and we recognize, we confess, that everything about us\r\n152: [00:17:37 -> 00:17:38] is weakness.\r\n153: [00:17:38 -> 00:17:39] You've chosen the weak things of this world,\r\n154: [00:17:39 -> 00:17:42] the base things that which is dead,\r\n155: [00:17:42 -> 00:17:44] that which is hopeless, that which is good for nothing.\r\n156: [00:17:44 -> 00:17:46] And you're saying, that's what I'm gonna use\r\n157: [00:17:46 -> 00:17:48] to manifest my power.\r\n158: [00:17:48 -> 00:17:52] So Lord, we bring our uselessness, our hopelessness,\r\n159: [00:17:52 -> 00:17:56] our lack of everything Lord to You\r\n160: [00:17:56 -> 00:17:58] and so that You might prove Your power in our lives.\r\n161: [00:17:58 -> 00:18:00] Do that, Lord.\r\n162: [00:18:00 -> 00:18:02] You know our problems, you know our difficulties.\r\n163: [00:18:02 -> 00:18:04] You know the burdens we've been carrying\r\n164: [00:18:04 -> 00:18:05] and we lay them at Your feet, Lord.\r\n165: [00:18:05 -> 00:18:09] Burdens for ourselves, our spiritual battles,\r\n166: [00:18:09 -> 00:18:11] our emotional battles, our physical battles.\r\n167: [00:18:11 -> 00:18:13] You know them better than even we do.\r\n168: [00:18:13 -> 00:18:15] You knew we would face it before we even faced it.\r\n169: [00:18:15 -> 00:18:18] So we thank You and we proclaim that You are God\r\n170: [00:18:18 -> 00:18:22] who sees in the darkness, even when nobody else sees.\r\n171: [00:18:22 -> 00:18:24] You know the God who heals, you're the God who restores,\r\n172: [00:18:24 -> 00:18:26] you're the God who redeems.\r\n173: [00:18:26 -> 00:18:28] If You wouldn't spare Your only Son, Jesus,\r\n174: [00:18:28 -> 00:18:31] how much more will You not give us all that we need\r\n175: [00:18:31 -> 00:18:32] for life and godliness.\r\n176: [00:18:32 -> 00:18:34] We thank You, Lord, that You will do that.\r\n177: [00:18:34 -> 00:18:35] We proclaim our faith, Lord.\r\n178: [00:18:35 -> 00:18:37] I pray that every one of us from the youngest\r\n179: [00:18:37 -> 00:18:40] to the oldest will receive faith today.\r\n180: [00:18:40 -> 00:18:42] Faith that overcomes the world.\r\n181: [00:18:42 -> 00:18:44] Faith that triumphs in every circumstance, Lord.\r\n182: [00:18:44 -> 00:18:48] A living faith, a faith that is fixed its eyes\r\n183: [00:18:48 -> 00:18:50] on the hope that You've given us.\r\n184: [00:18:50 -> 00:18:52] So we confess our hope, Lord, and we proclaim\r\n185: [00:18:52 -> 00:18:54] that we will trust You this week.\r\n186: [00:18:54 -> 00:18:58] More than we have, Jesus, Jesus, how we've proved you, Lord.\r\n187: [00:18:58 -> 00:19:01] We look back on the past and we see how You've been faithful.\r\n188: [00:19:01 -> 00:19:02] You brought us through the circumstance\r\n189: [00:19:02 -> 00:19:03] and we thought we would never come through.\r\n190: [00:19:03 -> 00:19:05] And here we are this morning.\r\n191: [00:19:05 -> 00:19:07] We don't deserve to have life.\r\n192: [00:19:07 -> 00:19:10] And yet You've given us breath one more day, Lord, Jesus.\r\n193: [00:19:10 -> 00:19:11] You don't give us what we deserve.\r\n194: [00:19:11 -> 00:19:13] You give us life.\r\n195: [00:19:13 -> 00:19:15] Thank You, Lord, undeserving as we are now\r\n196: [00:19:15 -> 00:19:16] that You've given us life.\r\n197: [00:19:16 -> 00:19:19] Now that we see Jesus Christ and the hope that is in Him,\r\n198: [00:19:19 -> 00:19:21] how much more, Lord, all the earthly needs that we did.\r\n199: [00:19:21 -> 00:19:25] We need, Lord, all the earthly needs that we have.\r\n200: [00:19:25 -> 00:19:25] Thank You.\r\n201: [00:19:25 -> 00:19:27] Thank You for that promise.\r\n202: [00:19:27 -> 00:19:30] Your heavenly Father knows.\r\n203: [00:19:30 -> 00:19:31] Thank You for that promise, Lord,\r\n204: [00:19:31 -> 00:19:33] that our heavenly Father knows what we need.\r\n205: [00:19:33 -> 00:19:35] Knows that we need these things.\r\n206: [00:19:35 -> 00:19:37] So, Lord, I pray You'll free us from anxiety,\r\n207: [00:19:37 -> 00:19:39] free us from worry.\r\n208: [00:19:39 -> 00:19:40] Free us from unbelief, Lord Jesus.\r\n209: [00:19:40 -> 00:19:43] Speak your words to us this morning,\r\n210: [00:19:43 -> 00:19:44] even now as we're praying to You,\r\n211: [00:19:44 -> 00:19:46] as we're listening to Your voice,\r\n212: [00:19:46 -> 00:19:47] that we might receive faith.\r\n213: [00:19:47 -> 00:19:50] Faith comes from hearing Your voice, Lord Jesus.\r\n214: [00:19:50 -> 00:19:51] I believe You'll give us faith.\r\n215: [00:19:51 -> 00:19:54] So we pray for every individual, anyone that's\r\n216: [00:19:54 -> 00:19:55] in a spiritual battle.\r\n217: [00:19:55 -> 00:19:57] Somebody 